    "title": "1655 Carla Ridge in Photos - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Demetrius Simms ,\n5 hours ago The single-story residence is offered turnkey, with all its furnishings and custom lighting. Click here for the full story .\n1.\nThe 6,500-square-foot home is tucked behind wood-slatted fencing and a motorized driveway gate.\n2.\nA serene reflection pool sits alongside the front door.\n3.\nThe light-filled foyer, with a wavy front cabinet by design legend Paul Evans.\n4.\nThe living room includes one of the home’s four fireplaces.\n5.\nA custom light fixture by L.A. artist David Wiseman hangs above the sunken TV lounge.\n6.\nThe kitchen features cerused rift oak cabinetry and quartzite countertops.\n7.\nThe dining room spills onto an alfresco dining terrace with open views over the landscape.\n8.\nThe primary bedroom.\n9.\nThe primary bathroom.\n10.\nNatural light illuminates the makeup vanity.\n11.\nThe powder room features a mirror by David Wiseman.\n12.\nThe home office is lined with floating shelves.\n13.\nThe wine cellar.\n14.\nThe fitness room.\n15.\nA sunken lounge is almost entirely surrounded by the zero-edge pool.\n16.\nA fire pit keeps owners warm after sunset.\nView Full Gallery (16 Photos)",
    "summary": "5 hours ago The single-story residence is offered turnkey, with all its furnishings and custom lighting. The 6,500-square-foot home is tucked behind wood-slatted fencing and a motorized driveway gate. The light-filled foyer, with a wavy front cabinet by design legend Paul Evans. A custom light fixture by L.A. artist David Wiseman hangs above the sunken TV lounge. The kitchen features cerused rift oak cabinetry and quartzite countertops.",
